### Detailed Solution


### Step 1: Calculate moles of \(O_{2}\) evolved during Cu deposition

According to Faraday's first law of electrolysis, the equivalents of substances produced at electrodes are equal.
Equivalents of Cu = Equivalents of \(O_{2}\)
\frac{\text{mass of Cu}}{\text{equivalent weight of Cu}} = \frac{\text{moles of } O_{2}}{\text{n-factor of } O_{2}}
\frac{300\times 10^{-3}\text{ g}}{63.54/2 \text{ g/eq}} = n_{O_{2}}\times 4
\frac{300\times 10^{-3}\times 2}{63.54} = n_{O_{2}}\times 4
9.4428 \times 10^{-3} = n_{O_{2}}\times 4
n_{O_{2}} = \frac{9.4428 \times 10^{-3}}{4} = 2.3607 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol}

### Step 2: Calculate moles of \(O_{2}\) evolved when current is further passed

When current is further passed, only \(O_{2}\) is evolved as \(Cu^{2+}\) is exhausted.
Charge passed (Q) = current (I) \(\times\) time (t)
Q = 600\times 10^{-3}\text{ A} \times 28\text{ min} \times 60\text{ s/min}
Q = 1008\text{ C}
From the reaction \(O_{2}(g)+4H^{+}+4e^{-} \to 2H_{2}O\), 4 moles of electrons are required to produce 1 mole of \(O_{2}\).
Moles of electrons = \(\frac{Q}{F}\)
\text{Moles of electrons} = \frac{1008\text{ C}}{96500\text{ C/mol}} = 0.0104456 \text{ mol}
Since 4 moles of electrons produce 1 mole of \(O_{2}\):
n_{O_{2}} = \frac{\text{Moles of electrons}}{4} = \frac{0.0104456}{4} = 2.6114 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol}

### Step 3: Calculate total moles of \(O_{2}\) released

Total \(O_{2}\) released = \(n_{O_{2}}(\text{from Cu deposition}) + n_{O_{2}}(\text{from further current})\)
\text{Total } n_{O_{2}} = (2.3607 \times 10^{-3}) + (2.6114 \times 10^{-3})
\text{Total } n_{O_{2}} = 4.9721 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol}

### Step 4: Calculate total volume of \(O_{2}\) at STP

Molar volume at STP = 22.4 L/mol = 22400 mL/mol
\text{Total Volume of } O_{2} = \text{Total } n_{O_{2}} \times \text{Molar volume at STP}
\text{Total Volume of } O_{2} = 4.9721 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol} \times 22400 \text{ mL/mol}
\text{Total Volume of } O_{2} = 111.37504 \text{ mL}

### Step 5: Round to nearest integer

The total volume of oxygen evolved at STP during the entire process, rounded to the nearest integer, is 111 mL.

